<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ranulf de Gernon, 4th Earl of Chester</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1153">1153</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Ranulf II, Earl of Chester</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ranulf de Gernon was earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chester">Chester</a> from 1129 to 1153 and a major figure in the civil war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-king-of-england">King Stephen</a> and the Empress Matilda. Seeking to control <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlisle">Carlisle</a> and the north-west, he seized Lincoln Castle and in 1141 helped capture Stephen at the Battle of Lincoln. He changed sides several times and died in 1153, reportedly poisoned.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ranulf-de-gernon-4th-earl-of-chester.jpg" alt="Ranulf de Gernon, 4th Earl of Chester" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edited by William Farrer and J. Brownbill, M.A. Archibald Constable and Company Limited · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Victoria_history_of_the_county_of_Lancaster_-_Ranulf_Gernons,_Earl_of_Chester,_1129-1153.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
